<title>UK: Rothschild says 10 bidders for UK housing loans.</title>
<headline>Rothschild says 10 bidders for UK housing loans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>N.M. Rothschild said on Tuesday it had received responses from 26 institutions forming 10 separate bidders who are seeking to pre-qualify for the proposed privatisation of up to 1.1 billion stg of loans to housing associations.</p>
<p>The loans are currently owned by three corporations regulating housing associations, The Housing Corporation, Scottish Homes and Housing for Wales.</p>
<p>Rothschild, acting as financial adviser to the Department of the Environment on the sale, said government ministers are expected to make a decision on the sale in October.</p>
</text>
